1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,043
Neighborline is a hotline for
neighborhood mutual-aid groups:

2
00:00:05,043 --> 00:00:11,276
the volunteers who get cash to neighbors
after a storm, a fire or a lost paycheck.

3
00:00:11,276 --> 00:00:13,985
Today that runs on English web forms,

4
00:00:13,985 --> 00:00:18,195
comment threads and one
volunteer's personal Venmo.

5
00:00:18,195 --> 00:00:22,203
It's slow, it shuts out people
who can't fill in the form,

6
00:00:22,203 --> 00:00:24,100
and it's easy to impersonate.

7
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:28,352
So a neighbor just leaves a
voice note, in any language.

8
00:00:28,352 --> 00:00:32,085
AI transcribes it,
translates it and reads it back.

9
00:00:32,085 --> 00:00:35,585
The group's written rules,
as code, set the amount.

10
00:00:35,585 --> 00:00:41,474
Two organizers approve with passkeys, and
PayPal Payouts sends the money to PayPal

11
00:00:41,474 --> 00:00:46,800
or Venmo. The AI never decides who
gets help, and never touches the money.

12
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:51,605
Two days after the ice storm,
the Eastside is still dark.

13
00:00:51,605 --> 00:00:57,800
Mrs. Lan is seventy-one. Her heat is off,
and her phone is at twenty-three percent.

14
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:07,400
[Mrs. Lan, in Vietnamese] “Hello, I’m Mrs. Lan, from the
Eastside. After the ice storm,
my house has been without
power for two days now.”

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,500
She left a voice note,
in Vietnamese. Watch the clock.

16
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:17,809
She heard it read back in
Vietnamese and said yes.

17
00:01:17,809 --> 00:01:24,003
The group's own rules, not the AI, set
the amount: a hundred and fifty dollars.

18
00:01:24,003 --> 00:01:25,600
Two organizers sign.

19
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:32,481
Paid, into her Venmo,
with a message in Vietnamese.

20
00:01:32,481 --> 00:01:38,443
Twenty-two point five seconds to the
SUCCESS webhook, on our PayPal stand-in.

21
00:01:38,443 --> 00:01:42,800
The approvals came on cue;
real neighbors take longer.

22
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:49,000
Rosa asks for groceries, in Spanish.
Same rules, two approvals.

23
00:01:51,002 --> 00:01:55,105
Her email has no PayPal
account yet: unclaimed.

24
00:01:55,105 --> 00:01:57,802
She gets claim help in Spanish.

25
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:03,536
She claims it. Success. Most
payout systems stop at unclaimed;

26
00:02:03,536 --> 00:02:05,100
this one follows through.

27
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:10,307
Someone posing as the organizers,
with a Venmo handle one letter off?

28
00:02:10,307 --> 00:02:14,850
Approve is disabled on
every phone. No money moves.

29
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:20,488
Under the hood: the agents that talk
to neighbors have no PayPal tools.

30
00:02:20,488 --> 00:02:24,756
One separate approval service
holds the Payouts credentials,

31
00:02:24,756 --> 00:02:30,000
and it pays only on a record signed with
the passkeys of two different organizers.

32
00:02:30,450 --> 00:02:35,558
For agent builders: the same
guard ships as an MCP server.

33
00:02:35,558 --> 00:02:40,644
An AI agent asking to pay is refused
without two humans' signatures.

34
00:02:40,644 --> 00:02:42,500
With them, it pays.

35
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:47,601
That night, one window on
the Eastside is warm again.

36
00:02:47,601 --> 00:02:53,591
Neighborline is open source. Try the
hotline yourself; the link is below.

37
00:02:53,591 --> 00:02:57,800
Because the morning after a storm,
help should sound like your own language.
